1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,280
Your AI agent can run a command. But real work happens in a terminal.

2
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:11,380
Servers that keep running. Prompts that wait for an answer. Jobs you have to stop.

3
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:19,020
Meet termctl: an MCP server that gives any agent real, persistent terminal sessions on your machine.

4
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:25,020
Sessions remember where they are, so each command picks up where the last one left off.

5
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:31,140
Start a dev server, keep reading its live output, and the agent never has to wait.

6
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:36,340
Type into a Python prompt, or press Control-C, just like you would.

7
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:44,900
Risky commands pause until you approve them, with one click, on your own machine. Attempts to self-approve are blocked.

8
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:52,660
It speaks standard MCP. We tested it end to end with Manus driving a real terminal on a Mac.

9
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:57,120
termctl. Give your agent a real terminal.
